(2. Recurrent Neural Networks \(RNN\) and LSTMs) Tj
0 -18 Td
(Recurrent Neural Networks introduced recurrent feedback loops allowing sequence memory.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(Vanishing and exploding gradient issues made long-range dependency capture difficult.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(Long Short-Term Memory \(LSTM\) networks addressed this with input, forget, and output gates.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(Gated Recurrent Units \(GRU\) simplified the architecture with reset and update gates.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(Sequence-to-sequence encoder-decoder frameworks laid the groundwork for modern models.) Tj
0 -18 Td
ET
endstream
